    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> became a republic on 26 January 1950, when the constitution drafted under B.R. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/b-r-ambedkar">Ambedkar</a> came into force.</li><li>It has remained a parliamentary democracy, interrupted only by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-emergency-india">Emergency</a> of 1975–1977, with regular elections since 1951–1952.</li><li>Now the world's most populous country, it is a nuclear power and one of the five largest economies by nominal output.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The first general election of 1951–1952 had about 173 million voters, most unable to read, so each party was given a symbol, a practice Indian elections still use.</p></aside>
    </section>

